[statement]
Observed; the rule is not yet known in full. As
`a-candidate-whose-dependency-cannot-be-met-is-passed-over-beside-one-depending-on-the-first-of-two-requirers`,
with `n` 1 needing `y`, the second of the two packages that need `q`:
apk chooses `n` 2 and refuses. Two requested names show the same where
the one first in name order needs `q` itself and the other needs it
through `z`, and `n` 1 needs `z`: apk refuses whichever order the request
states them in.

[repository]
P:top
V:1
D:z y

P:z
V:1
D:q

P:y
V:1
D:q

P:q
V:1
D:n

P:n
V:2
D:missing

P:n
V:1
D:y

[request]
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   missing (no such package):
|     required by: n-2[missing]
refused
